    "['map vlan [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm domain md1 level 6 service ma1 vlan 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent for the Huawei `map vlan 10` command:\\n\\n##\\nethernet cfm domain md1 level 6 service ma1 vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco command:\\n1. Creates the CFM domain (md1) at level 6\\n2. Associates the maintenance association (ma1) \\n3. Maps it to VLAN 10, similar to Huawei's functionality\\n\\nThe command combines the domain/service creation with the VLAN mapping in Cisco's syntax, where these operations are typically configured together rather than as separate commands like in Huawei.\", 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm domain md1 level 6 service ma1 vlan 10'}]]": 1,
